Package: DBinventory
Title: Inventory and Column Profile of a Database or Parquet Store
Version: 0.1.1
Authors@R: 
    person("Tom", "Smith", , "tomsmith_uk@hotmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Builds the first two artefacts of a data-documentation effort from
    a read-only connection: an inventory of every table and column (schema,
    name, type, row count, size, newest datetime, when profiled) and a per-column
    profile (null rate, distinct count, min and max, top values, inferred
    semantic type, uniqueness, fingerprint hashes). Works against any 'DBI'
    connection with dialect support for Microsoft SQL Server, DuckDB (including
    Parquet files and directories), SQLite and PostgreSQL. Results are written
    to a SQLite store with per-table checkpointing so long runs can resume, and
    can be exported to CSV or Parquet and rendered as a Quarto report.
